    "problem_statement": "### Issue with Class Pickling in Cloudpickle\n\n#### Describe the Issue\n\nAfter a recent update, it seems that there is an issue with pickling classes using `cloudpickle`. The problem arises when attempting to pickle classes that have certain attributes or are dynamically generated. This behavior was not present in previous versions and is causing unexpected failures.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\nTo reproduce the issue, you can try pickling a dynamically generated class or a class with specific attributes like `__annotations__` or `__slots__`. Here's a simple example:\n\n```python\nimport cloudpickle\n\nclass DynamicClass:\n    __slots__ = ['attr1', 'attr2']\n    __annotations__ = {'attr1': int, 'attr2': str}\n\n    def __init__(self, attr1, attr2):\n        self.attr1 = attr1\n        self.attr2 = attr2\n\ninstance = DynamicClass(1, 'test')\n\n# Attempt to pickle the instance\npickled_instance = cloudpickle.dumps(instance)\n```\n\n#### Expected Results\n\nThe class instance should be pickled without any errors.\n\n#### Actual Results\n\nAn error is raised during the pickling process, indicating issues with handling certain class attributes or dynamic class generation.\n\n#### Additional Information\n\nThis issue seems to affect a variety of test cases related to class pickling, including those involving abstract base classes, dataclasses, and classes with type hints. It would be helpful if someone could look into this and confirm whether this is a bug or if there are any changes in the expected behavior of `cloudpickle`. Thank you!"
